# 5. Random question engine

Whenever a player begins a new round:

1. Load the currently enabled questions.
2. Select five suitable questions.
3. Avoid repeats inside the same round.
4. Prefer questions that the same browser has not seen in recent games.
5. Randomise question order.
6. Shuffle answer choices when appropriate.
7. Preserve correct-answer mapping after shuffling.

Use a rolling recent-question history. A reasonable target is to avoid the last 20 questions played on the same browser when enough eligible questions exist.

If the repository has fewer eligible questions than required, relax the recent-history restriction gradually rather than preventing a game from starting.

Aim for each round to include at least one cricket question, one aviation question and one personalised Advik question. Vary the remaining selection so every round doesn't follow the same pattern.

Do not secretly reuse one fixed group of five questions. Do not repeat a question within one round.

